        "original_id": "525e4bf8-32f7-56b1-bd42-7871b4256eb9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Minneapolis–Saint Paul International Airport, Cheyenne Regional Airport, Little Rock, Cheyenne, Laramie County, Wyoming\n- Products: Pinnacle Airlines Flight 3701\n- Concepts: civil-military airports, joint civil-military public use international airports, repositioning flights\n\nFacts:\n- Minneapolis–Saint Paul International Airport is also known as Wold–Chamberlain Field.\n- Minneapolis–Saint Paul International Airport is a joint civil-military public use international airport.\n- Cheyenne Regional Airport is also called Jerry Olson Field.\n- Cheyenne Regional Airport is a civil-military airport one mile north of downtown Cheyenne in Laramie County, Wyoming.\n- Pinnacle Airlines Flight 3701 was an overnight repositioning flight with no passengers from Little Rock, Arkansas, to Minneapolis–Saint Paul International Airport.\n- Both crew members on Pinnacle Airlines Flight 3701 were killed.",
